part wcp_2
  tally 1
  law
  note "WCP-2 · Tax on contributions: the employer's contributions are the employee's employment income on the day the employer pays them to the plan, outside the SOC-1 and SOC-2 bases (.1); the employee's are deducted from pay after tax and contributions (.2); nothing is taxed while units stay in the plan (.3)."

source wcp_2 "Workplace Capital Plans Act, WCP-2 Tax on contributions (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version wcp2_v1
  cite wcp_2
  governs 2019-07-01..
  known 2019-01-15
  note "WCP-2 v1, in force 2019-07-01 until replaced, published 2019-01-15; governs pay paid from 2019-07-01."
